ber>9293639</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1137019A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NARAYA KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON CHEMICON</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARAYA, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON CHEMI-CON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NARAYA KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARAYA, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A cathode foil is produced by forming a TiN film on an etched aluminum foil by cathode arc plasma deposition, and an anode foil is produced by forming a dielectric coating on an etched aluminum foil by a conventional chemical conversion.  The anode foil, the cathode foil and a separator are wound together to form a capacitor element assembly, which is then impregnated with an EDT monomer and then with a butanol solution of 40% to 60% of ferric paratoluenesulfonate and heated at 20 to 180  DEG C for more than 30 minutes.  Then, the capacitor element assembly is coated with resin and aged.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>D'après cette invention, la feuille de la cathode est obtenue en formant un film de TiN sur une feuille d'aluminium gravée selon un procédé de déposition plasmique cathodique et à arc. La feuille de l'anode est quant à elle obtenue en formant un revêtement diélectrique sur une feuille d'aluminium gravée selon un procédé de conversion chimique traditionnel. La feuille de l'anode, la feuille de la cathode et un séparateur sont enroulés de manière à former un ensemble élément condensateur. Ce dernier est ensuite imprégné d'un monomère EDT puis d'une solution de butanol comprenant de 40 à 60 % de paratoluènesulfonate ferrique et, enfin, chauffé à une température de 20 à 180 DEG  C pendant plus de 30 minutes. L'ensemble élément condensateur est alors enduit d'une résine, puis vieilli.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>